From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:35:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: Queue G16 execution work on system_dfl_wq

system_unbound_wq is deprecated in v7.3, which warns once on the first
G16 submission. Use its replacement, the default unbound queue; the
execution work keeps the same unbound behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_drm.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_drm.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_drm.rs
index a2cbee5070b2..602300c47470 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_drm.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_drm.rs
@@ -1355,7 +1355,7 @@ fn run(job: &mut sched::Job<Self>) -> Result<Option<dma_fence::Fence>> {
         }
         if !engine.running {
             engine.running = true;
-            let _ = workqueue::system_unbound().enqueue(execution.clone());
+            let _ = workqueue::system_dfl().enqueue(execution.clone());
         }
         // A running worker may be asleep waiting for firmware on another
         // queue. New ready work must wake it even if no GPU event arrives.
